for a while, and he told me that everybody in the course of the day, they would sit around and play volleyball, and they would appear to be just naturally very bright, and papers would show up up and calculations would get done. And then you said, if you went there at night, you'd realize in every office, people were staying up all night doing the work, but they didn't want to admit how hard they were working to anybody else. Is there a time in your life where you feel like you recall this happening to you? Where in some ways you could actually tell that it was persistence and grit, you know,

