thousands of moving parts, very subtle. So they said, well, you know, to fix a good airplane, it's not a question of how smart you are at math, but really the idea was the ability to kind of see the project as a whole, assess a situation. And part of that situation would also be a human situation, understanding in that case how the pilot would respond, understanding this in a broader way, in a more, I guess, inclusive way. And so they really developing kind of computer games to measure those characteristics and understand the ability to solve problems.

