Testing companies are starting to see what Jim says is clear from the data. Consciousness and other character skills play a huge role in success whether we're talking about a scientist at Los Alamos or a recent high school graduate. When we come back, how to develop these skills in the most disadvantaged kids and the extraordinary effect this can have on their lives. This can have on their lives. I'm Shankar Vedantam, you're listening to Hidden Brain. This is NPR. In 1963, Louis Durman Sparks got her first job as a teacher at the Perry Preschool Project.

