Jim Heckman has followed the kids who went through the Perry Preschool Project, they're now middle-aged, and he's followed what happened to their children. What he finds is that an early investment in disadvantaged kids and their parents can pay dividends across generations. I'm Shankar Vedantam, and you're listening to Hidden Brain. This is NPR. is NPR.

